{"title":"1980 AHSME Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A man walks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> miles due west, turns <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd96fce8011b053b9d83a5b2d39ec3c756f0f66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> to his left and walks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> miles in the new direction. If he finishes a a point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> from his starting point, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/4/7a450df7f921b83f2acf0ae3bd1faf0c617007cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} \\ \\sqrt 3 \\qquad \\text{(B)} \\ 2\\sqrt{5} \\qquad \\text{(C)} \\ \\frac 32 \\qquad \\text{(D)} \\ 3 \\qquad \\text{(E)} \\ \\text{not uniquely determined}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"543\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/22525c9bbb7cceb25bffa80093eb2b95250a5191.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  size(200); pair T=origin, H=(sqrt(3)*1.5, 0), F=(sqrt(3)*1.5, -1.5), S1=(sqrt(3), 0), S2=(2*sqrt(3), 0); draw(H--T--F--cycle); draw((-1,0)--(5,0)); draw(arc(F, sqrt(3), 0, 180)); label(&quot;$H$&quot;, H, SE); label(&quot;$\\ell$&quot;, (5,0), E); label(&quot;$T$&quot;, T, N); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, SE); label(&quot;$S_1$&quot;, S1, NW); label(&quot;$S_2$&quot;, S2, NE); label(&quot;$30^\\circ$&quot;, T, 1.5S+5.4E); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"125\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> be the line he was initially walking on, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be his turning point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be his finishing point, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />.  Since he turned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd96fce8011b053b9d83a5b2d39ec3c756f0f66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/b/d2b767f05d421429bc659b069cea76ddd9c70b3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle HTF = 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/1/a01e6143c45df3a508fccaf0a1c0e9f6357ce297.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HF = \\frac{3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" /> miles.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> miles from his starting point, his starting point lies on a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c77cf4b63af80bfbc6a9ad9b4b9e8e549e77d78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> miles centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/e/4ee3acc2c07a8b621afd976115c4f361b7349741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3}{2} &lt; \\sqrt{3} &lt; 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />, this circle must intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" /> once between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and once east of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4caea56d945d0b6e49701b42ce06e0fb92e663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> be these two intersections, respectively.  Both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b10d5ee88ffc7d59f9c282b366953fb4fa4051f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f4caea56d945d0b6e49701b42ce06e0fb92e663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"15\" /> are possible starting points, and clearly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/a/24a3ff9fc90ca800c935d623d878b54cce9e0d6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$TS_1 \\neq TS_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/704ceacca41ab1de37b94c4eb33026fe28a27b6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(\\textbf{E}) not uniquely determined}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"222\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/6/df60edd49930684aa24624dfbd33138f1abe7bf4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  size(320); pair T=origin, S1=(sqrt(3), 0), F=(sqrt(3)*1.5, -1.5); draw(S1--T--F--cycle); label(&quot;$S$&quot;, S1, NE); label(&quot;$T$&quot;, T, NW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F, SE); label(&quot;$x$&quot;, T--S1, N); label(&quot;$\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, S1--F, 0.6N+0.3E); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, T--F, SW); label(&quot;$30^\\circ$&quot;, T, 1.5S+5.4E);  pair T2=(3, 0), S2=(3+2*sqrt(3), 0), F2=(3+sqrt(3)*1.5, -1.5); draw(S2--T2--F2--cycle); label(&quot;$S$&quot;, S2, NE); label(&quot;$T$&quot;, T2, NW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;, F2, S); label(&quot;$\\sqrt{3}$&quot;, S2--F2, 0.1E); label(&quot;$x$&quot;, T2--S2, N); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, T2--F2, SW); label(&quot;$30^\\circ$&quot;, T2, 1.5S+5.4E); [/asy]\" width=\"535\" height=\"158\" />\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be his starting point, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the point where he turns, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be his finishing point.  Since he turned <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/995f44efd3d9791d3844223f8bd6b35c600050fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/e/fce982ce59f16c70890515982abfd755a8520e45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle STF = 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />.  By the Law of Cosines, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/3/403bb35ff0096ef9790f5dbea6c1953759a70f2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FS^2 = FT^2 + ST^2 - 2 \\cdot FT \\cdot ST \\cos \\angle STF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"343\" height=\"18\" />. That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/56198d2c06695fc7449a462bed993bbda0d3ad2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2 = 3^2 + x^2 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot x \\cdot \\cos 30^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"279\" height=\"37\" />.  Combining all terms on one side yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/b/78b3b6d00300adaecd07749fe3ebb171b6518ee3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - 3x\\sqrt{3} + 6 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"150\" height=\"21\" />, which factors as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd27db0b4af5525f6ef5445c7c19b351608e22db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(x - \\sqrt{3}\\right)\\left(x - 2\\sqrt{3}\\right) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"203\" height=\"34\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/d/11d08e821238d62375f1285baddce7b9e4a171ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/1/501111cdb69f120c95770d6d6dcbdc5d29861670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" /> are both possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/4/704ceacca41ab1de37b94c4eb33026fe28a27b6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(\\textbf{E}) not uniquely determined}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"222\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME\" title=\"1980 AHSME\">1980 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1980 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1980 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1980\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1980 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1980 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1980 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1980 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1980 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1980 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1980 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1980 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_AHSME_Probl